SWEET FB vsync period boot-arg (patch 0404, oriole speed round 2026-11-19; plan: match the kernel's vsync timer to the panel). Patch 0401 measured oriole's aftermarket panel TE at 58.23 Hz (period median 17172 us, min 17169, max 17175, three 1 s windows, run speed-base), while the emulated vsync tick (patches 0046/0101/0149) runs 16667 us = 60.00 Hz: about 1.8 panel copies per second are overwritten before the panel scans them, and CoreAnimation is told a 16.667 ms frame interval (the vsync notification's period word, patch 0101). Boot-arg sweetfb_vsync_us=US (8000..40000; absent or 0 = 16667 as before; outside = GAP line, default kept) sets the tick period used everywhere SWEET_FB_VSYNC_US was used (timer arm, absolute re-arm 0149, the period in the vsync notification, the 0190 resume). Software timer only: no register, no store to hardware. Phase is still free-running (no TE interrupt).
